{{also|greenlight|green-light}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From the standard red-green color scheme used in [[traffic light]]s and [[railway signal]]s.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-green light.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[traffic light]] in its green state (indicating that vehicles may proceed).
#: {{ux|en|The drive home was much faster than usual; somehow we managed to hit every '''green light'''.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} [[approval|Approval]], or [[permission|permission]] to [[proceed]].
#: {{ux|en|We have a '''green light''' on the project. Work starts today.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 May 20|title=Network News: Class 345s finally able to serve Heathrow Airport|journal=Rail|page=15|text=And Crossrail's Class 345 Aventra fleet finally has the '''green light''' to carry passengers to Heathrow Airport, after the Office of Rail and Road granted approval for the European Train Control System (ETCS) Level 2 overlay system.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[go-ahead]] to commit a [[crime]], specifically to carry out a hit on someone (i.e. to [[kill]]).
#: {{ux|en|Yo man, I heard someone had put a '''green light''' out on you, so watch your back.}}

